Since 30 = 2 × 3 × 5, an integer is relatively prime to 30 exactly when it is divisible by none of 2, 3, and 5. Among the 30 integers from 1 to 30, the odd ones not divisible by 5 are 1, 3, 7, 9, 11, 13, 17, 19, 21, 23, 27, and 29. Removing the multiples of 3 (3, 9, 21, and 27) leaves 12 − 4 = 8 favorable choices.
The probability is 8/30 = 4/15.
Final answer: \frac{4}{15}
